```

This solution works by reversing the operations: instead of multiplying or subtracting from `startValue` to reach `target`, it divides or adds to `target` to reach `startValue`. This approach is more efficient because it reduces the number of operations needed. When `target` is greater than `startValue`, if `target` is even, it can be halved (the reverse of doubling). If `target` is odd, it can be incremented (the reverse of decrementing). Once `target` is less than or equal to `startValue`, the only way to proceed is by subtracting 1 from `startValue` until it matches `target`.

